---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<Layout title="Privacy">
  <Header />

  <main class="container privacy">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>

    <p class="privacy__updated"><em>Last updated: 18 October 2026.</em></p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website is run by {siteConfig.businessName}, a UK handmade
      macramé business. This policy explains what happens to any
      information you share with us through this website.
    </p>

    <h2>What information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not have any sign-up, order or contact forms, so it
      does not collect or store any personal information about you directly.
      The buttons and links on this site either take you to an external
      platform (Etsy, Facebook or Instagram) or open an email to us in your
      own email app — in both cases, you choose what information to share
      and with whom.
    </p>

    <h2>Email enquiries</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact us by email at
      <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>,
      whatever you include in that email (such as your name, email address
      and details of your enquiry) is sent directly to our inbox. We only
      use this information to reply to you and to discuss your enquiry or
      order. We do not share it with third parties, and we do not use it for
      marketing unless you ask us to. We keep enquiry emails only for as
      long as reasonably needed to deal with your enquiry or order, and any
      related records we are required to keep for tax purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Shopping with us</h2>
    <p>
      Purchases are currently handled entirely through our
      <a href={siteConfig.etsyUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Etsy shop</a>.
      Etsy processes and stores information related to your order (such as
      payment and delivery details) under its own privacy policy, which
      applies in addition to this one.
    </p>

    <h2>Social media</h2>
    <p>
      Our <a href={siteConfig.facebookUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook</a>
      and <a href={siteConfig.instagramUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram</a>
      pages are hosted by Meta, not by us. If you message or interact with
      us there, that platform's own privacy policy applies to how it
      handles your information.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not use cookies, analytics or any tracking tools of
      its own.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This website is intended for adults and is not directed at children.
      We do not knowingly collect information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under UK data protection law, you have the right to ask what
      information we hold about you (if any), to ask us to correct it, or to
      ask us to delete it. To do this, just email us at
      <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time, for example if we add
      order or contact forms to the website in future. Any changes will be
      posted on this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions about this privacy policy, please email
      <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-block: 2rem 3rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .privacy__updated {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
